{
  "documents": [
    {
      "title": "Agreed design scope",
      "text": "Design quote accepted by buyer: 14 May\nSeller: Lina Dalisay, independent designer, Philippines\nBuyer: Mara Venn, owner of fictional shop Pebble Fern\nFee: USD 480, payable through PayPal\n\nDeliver one primary logo in color and black-and-white versions.\nDeliver three social media templates in editable format.\nDeliver a brand guidelines PDF with color and typography specifications.\nDeliver the final logo as a vector file.\n\nThe fee covers one round of revisions to the selected concept. The buyer will supply the shop name and preferred colors. Final files will be sent by email after approval of the concept. Any additional formats or design work will require a separate quote."
    },
    {
      "title": "Design handover note",
      "text": "Handover from Lina to Mara, 28 May\n\nThe approved design files have been sent in the delivery folder. Please download them within 30 days and let me know if you have trouble opening anything.\n\nFile list:\n- Primary logo: color and black-and-white versions, PNG files\n- Social media template 1: editable\n- Social media template 2: editable\n- Primary logo: vector SVG file\n\nThe third template is not in this handover. I will send it separately when it is ready. The brand guidelines PDF was attached to my earlier email; please check that message. The two templates included here use the approved palette and can be adapted for different posts."
    },
    {
      "title": "Post-delivery chat",
      "text": "28 May, 10:12 — Mara: I downloaded the folder. The color and black-and-white logos look good, and the SVG opens on my computer.\n\n28 May, 10:18 — Lina: Great, thanks for checking those. The two editable templates are in the same folder.\n\n28 May, 10:24 — Mara: Yes, I can edit both. I was expecting three templates, though.\n\n28 May, 10:31 — Lina: You're right. The third is still being prepared and wasn't included today. I'll message you when I send it.\n\n28 May, 10:40 — Mara: Please do. I'll also look through my earlier emails for the guidelines."
    }
  ],
